I'm leaning towards option 2.

During the implementation of EvenPodsSpread, the predicate metadata is extremely important to support not only its core function but also preemption. Upon migration to the scheduler framework, a pre-processed metadata is still inevitable to serve as fact-of-truth of that Filter Plugin.

@draveness Basically some simply plugins don't need the metadata too much, but some ones such as EvenPodsSpread and PodAffinity need to pre-know the state of the whole cluster (as they're related with topology domains rather than just nodes).
